    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0254" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg254"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr.
                            Dayton</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 21, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of September 30 (No. 55) has
                    been received. I thank you for your diligence in transmitting the papers
                    concerning our <pb facs="0255" n="255" xml:id="pg255"/> blockade, which it
                    contains. The blockade is already very effective, quite as much so as any nation
                    ever established. Proceedings are now on foot which will remove the premature
                    objections of the French consul to which you allude.</p>
                <p>I am your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
